etrical deviations along both axes, assisting in differentiating asymmetric shapes.\ndf['SKEWNESS_DIFFERENCE'] = df['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS'] - df['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS']", "# KURTOSIS_INTERACTION\n# Product of Kurtosis About Major Axis and Kurtosis About Minor Axis.\n# Usefulness: Amplifies extreme deviations in axis shapes, helping highlight unique geometric patterns in vehicles.\ndf['KURTOSIS_INTERACTION'] = df['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS'] * df['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS']", "# MAX_LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY_SQ\n# Square of Max Length Rectangularity.\n# Usefulness: Captures prominent nonlinear geometric patterns associated with the maximum bounding rectangle dimensions.\ndf['MAX_LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY_SQ'] = df['MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY']  2", "# SCALED_RADIUS_TO_COMPACTNESS\n# Ratio of Scaled Radius of Gyration to Compactness.\n# Usefulness: Emphasizes how radius spread relates to compactness, useful to identify tightly packed silhouettes relative to spread.\ndf['SCALED_RADIUS_TO_COMPACTNESS'] = df['SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION'] / df['COMPACTNESS']", "# CIRCULARITY_BIN\n# Binning Circularity into discrete intervals (Low, Medium, High).\n# Usefulness: Categorizes circular resemblance thresholds for simpler pattern capture among vehicle types.\ndf['CIRCULARITY_BIN'] = pd.cut(df['CIRCULARITY'], bins=[0, 40, 50, 60], labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High'])", "# GROUPBY_VEHICLE_TYPE_MEAN_COMPACTNESS\n# Mean Compactness within each vehicle class (target encoding).\n# Usefulness: Encodes class-level Compactness aggregation, capturing distinct compactness traits per vehicle type.\ndf['GROUPBY_VEHICLE_TYPE_MEAN_COMPACTNESS'] = df.groupby('vehicle_type')['COMPACTNESS'].transform('mean')", "df.drop(columns=['CIRCULARITY_BIN'], inplace=True)"]
